{"name":"Letter Jacket","hex":"#b8860b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"letter jacket","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A jacket traditionally worn by high-school and college students to represent school and team pride or to display their athletic or academic awards."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/letter_jacket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Letterman (sports)","blocks":[{"text":"In sports or activities in the United States, a letterman is a high school or college student who has met a specified level of participation or performance on a varsity team."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Letter_jackets%2C_Rome%2C_GA.jpg/330px-Letter_jackets%2C_Rome%2C_GA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Letterman_(sports)","wikidata":"Q6533680"},{"title":"Jacket","blocks":[{"text":"A jacket is a garment for the upper body, usually extending below the hips. A jacket typically has long or short sleeves and fastens in the front or slightly on the side. Jackets without sleeves are vests. A jacket is generally lighter, tighter-fitting, and less insulating than a coat, but both are outerwear. Some jackets are fashionable, while some others serve as protective clothing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Jacket2-1.jpg/330px-Jacket2-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacket","wikidata":"Q849964"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Traditional_Block_Letter_R_with_Embroidered_Mascot.gif/330px-Traditional_Block_Letter_R_with_Embroidered_Mascot.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Traditional_Block_Letter_R_with_Embroidered_Mascot.gif/330px-Traditional_Block_Letter_R_with_Embroidered